{"connection_id": "BC-3dc0803bfe4e68bc2fff", "ref": "Augustine, Confessions 13.9.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love as the weight that carries", "note": "Augustine calls love a person's weight, the force that carries one toward one's destination; this Christian interpretation turns the commentary's physical load and road into an account of moral desire."}
{"connection_id": "BC-391467a0995b28f2bc86", "ref": "Didache 16:5", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endure in faith through trial", "note": "The commentary joins trust and patience on a hard route; the Didache says those who endure in faith through an impending trial will be saved."}
{"connection_id": "BC-900bf8be1c5a7486ceea", "ref": "Gospel of Thomas 90", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "gentle yoke and promised rest", "note": "The commentary contrasts an exhausting load with one that can be carried; this saying invites people under an easy yoke and promises rest, a second Christian form of the burden image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2faf39c4f8d44a8d0193", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.10.13", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "temptation within capacity", "note": "Paul says God will not let testing exceed what people can bear and provides a way through it; this extends the commentary's concern with overloading from an animal to moral endurance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-098e8503ed4203efb9bc", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.10.13", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "trial within human capacity", "note": "The commentary's excessive driver imposes what a beast cannot bear; Paul says God will not allow a test beyond capacity and will supply a way to endure it."}
{"connection_id": "BC-181fc2e34e3ef6f6b168", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.15.58", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "labor in the Lord is not vain", "note": "Paul urges steadfastness and abundant work because labor in the Lord is not in vain; this answers the surah's loss language with a specific claim about enduring work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f064eb097784b89c6ab4", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.15.58", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "work and labor not in vain", "note": "The commentary asks whether human labor ends in loss; Paul urges steadfast work for the Lord on the ground that such labor is not in vain."}
{"connection_id": "BC-348179b36b24f9bfbb16", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.9.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "human worker shares the yield", "note": "Paul applies the threshing image to those who plow and thresh in hope of sharing the harvest; the verse explicitly moves from animal work to human labor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7242392a2725c5376763", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.9.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Paul reads ox law for laborers", "note": "The commentary moves from a working animal to human work; Paul explicitly interprets the unmuzzled ox rule as written for those who plow and thresh in hope."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dd9951e70baafa9aca5d", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.9.9", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "ox not muzzled at work", "note": "Paul quotes the command not to muzzle an ox threshing grain; the commentary's work-camel and working legs meet a text that protects an animal doing labor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0bf766b97416d757e0f7", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.9.9", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Paul cites the unmuzzled ox", "note": "The commentary reads a working animal beside human labor; Paul quotes the ox law and asks whether concern for oxen exhausts its meaning."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e55a8a1df7b17094b42b", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.2.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love prevents stumbling", "note": "The commentary praises safe travel without stumbling; the letter says one who loves a brother abides in light and has no cause for stumbling."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e364b7746db29782e649", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.3.18", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love in deed and truth", "note": "The commentary's good action becomes actual care rather than a label; the letter calls for love in deed and truth instead of words alone."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c9e9b7e3577467e1c4e8", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.5.3", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "commands not burdensome", "note": "The commentary opposes driving a creature under an intolerable load; this letter says God's commands are not burdensome for the loving believer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-249b04be13610cf22398", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.20", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endure while doing good", "note": "The commentary's good treatment and patience belong together; Peter values endurance under suffering for doing good, rather than suffering for wrongdoing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d6eea5e920ae59368ba4", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.24", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Christ bears sins", "note": "Peter says Christ bore sins in his body on the tree; this gives the load image a specific moral sense and a bearer who carries others' wrongdoing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-570da1d13ee533801c53", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.24", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "carried sins in his body", "note": "The commentary's losers carry their own burdens at the end; Peter says Christ bore sins in his body, altering who carries that moral weight."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cbf97c8ab02935c3062d", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.25", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "straying sheep returned to shepherd", "note": "The commentary's human road can lead to loss; after the claim that Christ bore sins, Peter calls his readers wandering sheep now returned to their shepherd."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b37d8825c170a4ffabc0", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.5.7", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "cast anxieties on God", "note": "Peter tells readers to cast their anxieties on God because he cares for them; this turns the human burden into a load entrusted to a caring bearer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1aea4ba24d9db6b89b37", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.1.3", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "work of faith and steadfastness", "note": "The letter remembers the work produced by faith and the steadfastness of hope; this closely joins the commentary's belief, deeds, and patience."}
{"connection_id": "BC-19eaf04a7fdc842effea", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Tim.5.18", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "ox and worker's wage", "note": "The commentary lets the animal's work illuminate human work; the letter joins the unmuzzled threshing ox to the worker's right to wages."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2d22c0ba3b1cc28518d3", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.1.8", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "burden beyond human strength", "note": "Paul says the affliction in Asia burdened the group beyond their strength and brought despair of life; this is a direct human counterpart to the commentary's load beyond capacity."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8d56f35935180f37ab5d", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.1.9", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "reliance redirected to God", "note": "Paul says the experience taught them not to rely on themselves but on God who raises the dead; this continues the beyond-capacity burden with a specific turn toward trust."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cffc8d11dac16b6222eb", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.4.17", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "light affliction and weight of glory", "note": "The commentary weighs a journey's burden against its final outcome; Paul sets momentary light affliction beside the immense lasting weight of glory it produces."}
{"connection_id": "BC-51a7723272bbb0249a91", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.5.4", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mortal person groans under burden", "note": "The commentary makes the human a burden bearer facing mortality; Paul describes people in an earthly tent as groaning while burdened and awaiting life beyond mortality."}
{"connection_id": "BC-acd7403a2bb3651adca3", "ref": "SBLGNT:2John.1.4", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walking in truth", "note": "The commentary places truth on a human route; the letter rejoices that some of its addressee's children are walking in truth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-957d59f3526fe84136e9", "ref": "SBLGNT:2John.1.6", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love as walking in commandment", "note": "The commentary turns good action into a route; the letter says love consists in walking according to God's commandments."}
{"connection_id": "BC-081fb8a0de3142a342fe", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.2.16", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Balaam's donkey rebukes him", "note": "The commentary criticizes a rider's harsh use of a mount; Peter retells Balaam's speaking donkey as a rebuke of the rider's wrongdoing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0c2a05a209d06c7d97b1", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.3.13", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "persist in doing good", "note": "The letter tells the community not to grow weary in doing good; it adds a direct communal exhortation to the commentary's mutual counsel toward patience."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0f1f2a19a60d78780580", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.7", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "finished race, kept faith", "note": "The commentary's traveler must carry faith through to the end; Paul says he has finished the race and kept the faith."}
{"connection_id": "BC-91a63a8a9c26a01c1e8e", "ref": "SBLGNT:3John.1.5", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faithful care for itinerant strangers", "note": "The commentary makes good treatment of a traveler concrete; the letter commends faithful work for visiting brothers, including strangers, before urging their onward journey."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b2a43bd720648c3f2cf9", "ref": "SBLGNT:3John.1.6", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "send travelers on worthily", "note": "The commentary values care for the one making a journey; the letter asks its hearer to send itinerant brothers onward in a manner worthy of God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9b67c77c4c7275beb03d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.15.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "unbearable yoke on necks", "note": "The commentary questions a load too hard for its bearer; Peter calls imposed observance a yoke that neither the ancestors nor his hearers could bear."}
{"connection_id": "BC-807a0d3ad7f6f12b3b85", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.15.28", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "no greater burden than necessary", "note": "The commentary distinguishes fitting loads from overloading; the council's letter explicitly limits the burden laid on Gentile believers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5e6983e48f836163e957", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.1.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bearing fruit in good work", "note": "The prayer asks that believers bear fruit in every good work; this directly resonates with the commentary's righteous deeds and its image of a productive worker."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6bc9700c36081f9a54bc", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.1.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "worthy walk bearing good work's fruit", "note": "The commentary joins a right road to effective work; the letter asks believers to walk worthily while bearing fruit in every good work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a055e78afda45ff58817", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.1.11", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "strength for endurance and patience", "note": "The next verse asks for strength to endure and be patient; it explicitly joins good work with the source's ṣabr."}
{"connection_id": "BC-facd381c7795f94cae9d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "created for good works", "note": "The next verse says believers are created in Christ for good works prepared for them; it reconnects faith and action while making works the result of grace."}
{"connection_id": "BC-24c1e992092c0adb65f0", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "good works prepared as a way to walk", "note": "The commentary places good action on the human journey; the letter says people are created for good works prepared beforehand so that they may walk in them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-749cd75852fa6c6d3181", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.8", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "saved by grace through faith", "note": "Ephesians says salvation is God's gift through faith and not from oneself; this differs in emphasis from the surah's joined condition of belief and righteous deeds."}
{"connection_id": "BC-81cd55813f7fcd00a5f4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.9", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "not from works", "note": "Ephesians explicitly excludes works as the basis for boasting; the contrast is about the ground of salvation, not a claim that the letter rejects ethical action."}
{"connection_id": "BC-655bd2e0a9b75a826a77", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.5.6", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith active through love", "note": "The commentary's trusted mount and good treatment put confidence beside action; Paul describes effective faith as working through love."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2e03cae5def2e490a58f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.5.7", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "running and obeying truth", "note": "The commentary joins the road to truth and endurance; Paul asks who obstructed people who had been running well from obeying the truth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7201c7ae3dacde914ace", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.2", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bear one another's burdens", "note": "Paul commands believers to carry one another's burdens; it turns load-bearing into mutual care, close to the source's mutual urging toward truth and patience."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d15301e4ef498ac966ef", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.2", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "carry one another's burdens", "note": "The commentary presents humans as bearers whose loads determine the journey; Paul makes mutual burden bearing a fulfillment of Christ's law."}
{"connection_id": "BC-64cb5fa557fc26ebfe4d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.5", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "each carries a load", "note": "Paul also says each person will carry their own load; beside 6:2, it distinguishes personal responsibility from burdens shared with others."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7b9b3ba7dfd74d856572", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.5", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "each carries own load", "note": "The commentary asks what load a person can properly carry; Paul also says each person will carry his own load, alongside his command to share burdens."}
{"connection_id": "BC-68b4492566b82a3ec675", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing good without growing weary", "note": "Paul tells believers not to grow weary in doing good, since they will reap if they do not give up; this closely joins righteous action, endurance, and outcome."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a8d882f07db9bab2880", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing good without weariness", "note": "The commentary joins good treatment with an unwearied journey; Paul urges persistence in doing good and promises a harvest if people do not give up."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a411ffd2c6f723884a5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "need for endurance", "note": "The audience needs endurance after doing God's will to receive what is promised; this joins action, patience, and final outcome."}

