{"connection_id": "BC-8d56f35935180f37ab5d", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.1.9", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "reliance redirected to God", "note": "Paul says the experience taught them not to rely on themselves but on God who raises the dead; this continues the beyond-capacity burden with a specific turn toward trust."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cffc8d11dac16b6222eb", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.4.17", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "light affliction and weight of glory", "note": "The commentary weighs a journey's burden against its final outcome; Paul sets momentary light affliction beside the immense lasting weight of glory it produces."}
{"connection_id": "BC-51a7723272bbb0249a91", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.5.4", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mortal person groans under burden", "note": "The commentary makes the human a burden bearer facing mortality; Paul describes people in an earthly tent as groaning while burdened and awaiting life beyond mortality."}
{"connection_id": "BC-acd7403a2bb3651adca3", "ref": "SBLGNT:2John.1.4", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walking in truth", "note": "The commentary places truth on a human route; the letter rejoices that some of its addressee's children are walking in truth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-957d59f3526fe84136e9", "ref": "SBLGNT:2John.1.6", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love as walking in commandment", "note": "The commentary turns good action into a route; the letter says love consists in walking according to God's commandments."}
{"connection_id": "BC-081fb8a0de3142a342fe", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.2.16", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Balaam's donkey rebukes him", "note": "The commentary criticizes a rider's harsh use of a mount; Peter retells Balaam's speaking donkey as a rebuke of the rider's wrongdoing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0c2a05a209d06c7d97b1", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.3.13", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "persist in doing good", "note": "The letter tells the community not to grow weary in doing good; it adds a direct communal exhortation to the commentary's mutual counsel toward patience."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0f1f2a19a60d78780580", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.7", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "finished race, kept faith", "note": "The commentary's traveler must carry faith through to the end; Paul says he has finished the race and kept the faith."}
{"connection_id": "BC-91a63a8a9c26a01c1e8e", "ref": "SBLGNT:3John.1.5", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faithful care for itinerant strangers", "note": "The commentary makes good treatment of a traveler concrete; the letter commends faithful work for visiting brothers, including strangers, before urging their onward journey."}
