{"connection_id": "BC-655bd2e0a9b75a826a77", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.5.6", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith active through love", "note": "The commentary's trusted mount and good treatment put confidence beside action; Paul describes effective faith as working through love."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2e03cae5def2e490a58f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.5.7", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "running and obeying truth", "note": "The commentary joins the road to truth and endurance; Paul asks who obstructed people who had been running well from obeying the truth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7201c7ae3dacde914ace", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.2", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bear one another's burdens", "note": "Paul commands believers to carry one another's burdens; it turns load-bearing into mutual care, close to the source's mutual urging toward truth and patience."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d15301e4ef498ac966ef", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.2", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "carry one another's burdens", "note": "The commentary presents humans as bearers whose loads determine the journey; Paul makes mutual burden bearing a fulfillment of Christ's law."}
