{"connection_id": "BC-7b9b3ba7dfd74d856572", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.5", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "each carries own load", "note": "The commentary asks what load a person can properly carry; Paul also says each person will carry his own load, alongside his command to share burdens."}
{"connection_id": "BC-68b4492566b82a3ec675", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing good without growing weary", "note": "Paul tells believers not to grow weary in doing good, since they will reap if they do not give up; this closely joins righteous action, endurance, and outcome."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a8d882f07db9bab2880", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing good without weariness", "note": "The commentary joins good treatment with an unwearied journey; Paul urges persistence in doing good and promises a harvest if people do not give up."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a411ffd2c6f723884a5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "need for endurance", "note": "The audience needs endurance after doing God's will to receive what is promised; this joins action, patience, and final outcome."}

