{"connection_id": "BC-66f6f3e80321fcca4808", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance to receive promise", "note": "The commentary's steep route requires patience until arrival; Hebrews says endurance is needed after doing God's will to receive the promise."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0a3b14ea8a76218d8fd2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.1", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "race with endurance", "note": "The audience is told to lay aside every weight and run with endurance; this combines the commentary's load, path, and patience in an athletic image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f108348909626dbdc628", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.1", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "run with endurance", "note": "The commentary's path and patience meet in the exhortation to lay aside hindering weight and run the appointed race with endurance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-79416a2ba8c8247c63ef", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.12", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "weak knees strengthened", "note": "The commentary describes a traveler whose legs work and may tire; Hebrews orders drooping hands and weak knees strengthened for continued movement."}
{"connection_id": "BC-63934481c81706d1631a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.13", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "straight paths and healed lame foot", "note": "The commentary's opened road and risk of stumbling meet the instruction to make straight paths for one's feet so the lame may be healed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-914bee91b876290e61ec", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.2", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Jesus endures cross for joy ahead", "note": "The commentary's bearer must endure a difficult route to its outcome; the runner is directed to Jesus, who endured the cross for the joy set before him."}
