{"connection_id": "BC-a860dd14977c1725d779", "ref": "WLC:Lev.16.21", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "iniquities placed on goat", "note": "The commentary's losers carry weights on their backs; Aaron places Israel's confessed sins on the live goat's head, turning guilt into a visible animal load."}
{"connection_id": "BC-eb7d251581eb20e68807", "ref": "WLC:Lev.16.22", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "goat bears sins into wilderness", "note": "The commentary's load and wilderness journey meet in the goat that bears the people's iniquities away to an uninhabited land."}
{"connection_id": "BC-580d7564b6eebf664af5", "ref": "WLC:Mic.4.2", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mountain ascent to learn walking paths", "note": "The commentary joins a steep destination to the way of right action; Micah's parallel oracle has nations ascend God's mountain to learn his ways and walk his paths."}
