{"connection_id": "BC-be997ba780100b5a808d", "ref": "WLC:Prov.12.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "righteous care for animals", "note": "The commentary glosses aslahtu as treating the animal well; Proverbs says a righteous person knows the needs of a beast, while the wicked person's compassion is cruel."}
{"connection_id": "BC-457e294f7c8cb1dcf05e", "ref": "WLC:Prov.12.10", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "righteous person and animal's life", "note": "The commentary glosses doing good as treating a beast well; the proverb makes the righteous person's concern for an animal's needs a test of righteousness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a4035237eb7a7f839900", "ref": "WLC:Prov.14.4", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "ox strength and harvest", "note": "The proverb says an empty manger is clean without oxen, but abundant crops come through the ox's strength; it names the cost and yield of animal labor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bd68172b1b0e88db3352", "ref": "WLC:Prov.27.23", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "know the state of the flock", "note": "The proverb tells the keeper to know the condition of his flock and attend to the herds; this makes the commentary's dependable animal and good treatment an ongoing duty of attention."}
{"connection_id": "BC-21a0334807ec0dea9490", "ref": "WLC:Prov.3.23", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walk securely without stumbling", "note": "The commentary praises a mount that will not stumble; the wisdom traveler is promised a secure way and an unslipping foot."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2c1cc91407d1a46acf0a", "ref": "WLC:Prov.3.5", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "trust beyond one's own understanding", "note": "The proverb commands trust in YHWH rather than reliance on one's own understanding; this makes the commentary's iman-as-reliability image a relation of dependence, not merely confidence in a mount."}
{"connection_id": "BC-02a2285dd660e067550b", "ref": "WLC:Prov.3.6", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "trust makes the path straight", "note": "The proverb says to acknowledge God in all one's ways and he will make the paths straight; it joins trust to the road image developed by the commentary."}

