+{"connection_id":"BC-cc23e2c74bc52c200476","ref":"WLC:Gen.24.19","status":"accepted","reason":"Rebekah offers water to the camels until they finish, the animal-care point stated in the linked Genesis 24 note.","paragraphs":[22],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.24.19","WLC:Gen.24.21","WLC:Gen.24.32"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6a2d766d49690fa5150e","ref":"WLC:Gen.24.19","status":"accepted","reason":"Watering the camels is explicit in Hebrew and helps distinguish actual care from the related root's prosperity meaning.","paragraphs":[22],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.24.19","WLC:Gen.24.21","WLC:Gen.24.32"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6485ec71089bb2ba39f3","ref":"WLC:Gen.24.21","status":"accepted","reason":"Hebrew צלח describes a journey's success beside the camels; the linked note states this differs from Arabic animal-care usage.","paragraphs":[22],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.24.19","WLC:Gen.24.21","WLC:Gen.24.32"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c24955d4c267634918c1","ref":"WLC:Gen.24.21","status":"accepted","reason":"The servant asks whether God prospered his way; the linked note situates this in the camel-watering journey and guards the lexical distinction.","paragraphs":[22],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.24.19","WLC:Gen.24.21","WLC:Gen.24.32"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-58a415bd4afea2460a87","ref":"WLC:Gen.24.32","status":"accepted","reason":"The Hebrew says the camels were unloaded and given straw and fodder; the linked note explicitly records that care.","paragraphs":[22],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.24.19","WLC:Gen.24.21","WLC:Gen.24.32"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-001"]}
*** End Patch"));

